# Practice

#### Let's try using an AI tool in a low-stress way. You’ve likely used AI technologies in the past, maybe even on a daily basis. For your first time working with AI in this series, you'll be using Code.org's integrated AI Chat program, **AI Chat Lab**.

## Introducing AI Chat Lab 

<img src="https://images.code.org/d82ce6ee4dc44c9d9ccdf68b2751fc1c-9fa6476e1e62030a0f0814bbc6f006b5-image-1700521543414 (2).png" alt="Code.org AI bot character" style="border-radius:40px; float: right; padding: 10px; height: 200px; clear: both; margin: 0 10px 10px 0;">

#### Code.org has created <strong>AI Chat Lab</strong>, a safe and student-friendly chatbot built directly into the Code.org's platform. This allows students and teachers to explore generative AI in an authentic and secure way without leaving the platform.

#### AI Chat Lab is designed specifically for education, so we’ve added guardrails to keep the experience safe and appropriate.</p>

* #### The chatbot supports learning in a guided, structured environment that encourages students to think critically as they work through problems.
* #### Content is monitored to ensure it remains appropriate and productive, making AI Chat Lab a safe space for exploration and discovery.

<br>
<p style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;"> ➡️ Want to know more about how AI Chat Lab works? Check out the <a href="https://support.code.org/hc/en-us/articles/30162711193741-AI-Chat-Lab-FAQ" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"> FAQ Support Article</a>.
</p>
<br>

#### During the AI 101 for Educators professional learning series you'll interact with a variety of AI tools including AI Chat Lab as well as external LLMs of your choice such as Gemini, Claude, or ChatGPT.

#### In the next level you'll interact with AI Chat Lab to learn more about AI.
